      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's heavy. \"a calm surrender.\" i guess that's what i'm struggling with. it's just that when i think about him finally letting go, it doesn't feel like a \"plot point\" anymore. it feels more like the only thing that actually makes sense. sometimes i look at my own life and it feels exactly like that gray space you mentioned. like i'm just waiting for the noise to stop too. do you really think a story is more \"true\" if the character just... gives up?",
