      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's weird how much that resonates. \"escaping the prison.\" that's exactly how it feels. like there's no point in trying to fix things when the struggle itself is what's killing you. if i write it the way you're saying, it feels less like i'm writing a tragedy and more like i'm just describing the only logical conclusion to a life like this. do you think it's more honest to tell the truth about that end than to force a resolution that isn't there?",
